# git-std hooks — post-changelog.hooks
#
# Runs after CHANGELOG.md is written, before staging and commit.
# Use for: linting or reformatting the changelog.
#
#   !  required   abort bump on failure
#   ?  advisory   warn on failure, never abort
#
# Examples:
#   ? some-linter CHANGELOG.md
#
# NOT prim. `/CHANGELOG.md` is in `.primignore` so that prim and `git std bump`
# do not fight over it once per release, and since 0.3.0 prim honours that
# ignore however it is invoked: `prim lint CHANGELOG.md` and
# `prim fmt CHANGELOG.md` both skip the file and say so. A prim line here would
# read as a gate and check nothing.
#
# `prim fmt --no-primignore CHANGELOG.md` would reach it, and is the wrong thing
# to reach for: it reformats the file the ignore exists to protect, which is the
# fight the entry prevents.
#
